  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>One thing to know first</h2>
      <p>According to the FAQ of the Le Lavandou tourist office, access to the beaches is banned to dogs, even on a lead, from 1 April to 31 October (assistance dogs excepted). The same FAQ names Var beaches that allow them on a lead: the easternmost part of Tamaris beach in La Londe-les-Maures, the pebble part of Cabasson beach in Bormes-les-Mimosas (to the west, towards the fort) and all the beaches of Ramatuelle. The campsites in the area, on the other hand, accept animals, under conditions specific to each site.</p>

      <h2>What the tourist office says</h2>
      <p>The tourist office's "Campings au Lavandou" page has an "Animals accepted" filter: seven campsites in the area answer "yes". The supplement, the size and number of dogs admitted, and access to the rentals (mobile homes, bungalows) are not given in this list: they depend on each campsite.</p>

      <h2>Where your dog can burn off energy</h2>
      <p>The "Caniludique du Grand Jardin" dog park, avenue de la Grande Bastide, offers 6,000 m² of free space with an agility course, free of charge. It is open from 8:30 am to 8 pm from 1 April to 31 October, and from 8:30 am to 6 pm from 1 November to 31 March (for example on Sunday 1 November 2026). Dogs must be identified, vaccinated, dewormed, treated against fleas and ticks, and stay under their owner's supervision; droppings must be picked up. The neighbouring Grand Jardin park itself is closed to dogs, even on a lead, according to the tourist office.</p>

      <h2>To check before you book</h2>
      <p>Conditions vary by campsite and by type of accommodation (pitch or rental): confirm by phone the supplement, the number of dogs and the rentals concerned before booking.</p>
